  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952: a contest for four aldermanic seats and twelve councillors returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 23 May 1952, p. 10; Londonderry Sentinel, 8 May 1952, p. 3). Twelve nominations for twelve councillor seats, no contest. The paper identifies Murphy (an aldermanic candidate), Brangan, McClements, John Christie and Fillis as Labour Party nominees; no other candidate carries a label. New members: Brangan, McClements, Tosh, Caldwell, Irwin and Hamilton. Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Londonderry Sentinel, 21 May 1955, p. 7 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the surname is recorded as Brangam (was Brangan); this paper (8 May 1952, p. 3) prints 'E. Brangan', kept in Name_As_Printed, but the 1955 return prints 'E. Brangam' as an outgoing member and the Belfast News-Letter, 2 March 1954, p. 8 names Councillor E. Brangam."
